      "notes": "Pending owner review; not an approval. New piece for the owner's 2026-10-20 request (\"we need a river fork also\"): the channel-cut base of the river_fork tile, a symmetric Y with river lanes on edges 0, 2 and 4 meeting at the centre. Bed: the river_straight profile at the distance to the nearest arm (the engine's river bed on this tile), the three wedges meeting on the bisector ridges; water to 4.0 m from each axis and 4.62 m from the centre on the bisectors (a widened pool), about 6 m of meadow to the grass edges. Every River edge carries river_straight_base's ring and joint row, so seams with river tiles match. Built by _river.build_base on the \"fork\" layout (_river_fork.py) with _river_flat's flattened meadow relief. Tris LOD0/1/2 3432/1260/354. Review docs/checkpoints/river_fork/sheet.jpg. The controller records the owner's decision."
